NAME
       crypto - hashes, ciphers and signatures

SYNOPSIS
       #include <crypto.h>

       void sha256(const void *d, size_t n, uint8_t out[32]);
       void sha512(const void *d, size_t n, uint8_t out[64]);
       void hmac_sha256(const uint8_t *key, size_t klen,
                        const uint8_t *msg, size_t mlen, uint8_t out[32]);
       void hkdf_extract(...);   void hkdf_expand(...);
       void pbkdf2_hmac_sha256(...);

       void chacha20_poly1305_encrypt(...);
       int  chacha20_poly1305_decrypt(...);
       void aes_gcm_encrypt(...);
       int  aes_gcm_decrypt(...);

DESCRIPTION
       The cipher suite behind TLS, SSH and crypt(1): SHA-256 and
       SHA-512, HMAC, HKDF and PBKDF2; ChaCha20-Poly1305 and AES-GCM;
       X25519 key agreement; Ed25519 and ECDSA signatures over P-256
       and P-384; and RSA.

       The AEAD decrypt functions verify the tag and return failure
       without producing plaintext, so tampering is detected rather
       than passed on.

       Every primitive is checked against the RFC and NIST test
       vectors.

RETURN VALUE
       Decrypt and verify functions return 0 on success and non-zero
       when authentication fails.

SEE ALSO
       tls(3), crypt(1), ssh(1), ssh-keygen(1)
